   "source": [
    "#### Retrieve document urls by Key (resolvedUrl)\n",
    "We build a nested list where each inner list contains the `resolvedUrl` values from the dictionaries in one documentLinkSet row of `df`. We loops over every index in `df[\"documentLinkSet\"]` and extracts `doc['resolvedUrl']` for each document."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "d90db020",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "document_retrieved = [\n",
    "    [doc[\"resolvedUrl\"] for doc in df[\"documentLinkSet\"][i]]\n",
    "    for i in range(len(df[\"documentLinkSet\"]))\n",
    "]\n",
    "# rich.print(document_retrieved)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "42094b1b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Sanitize the url to only get `*.pdf` files"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c53bc75c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pdf_links = [\n",
    "    url\n",
    "    for sublist in document_retrieved\n",
    "    for url in sublist\n",
    "    if url.lower().split(\"?\")[0].endswith(\".pdf\")\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "rich.print(pdf_links)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8e14019",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We download using the `download` module. (CAUTION: it will download over `1000` pdf docs)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2bb51650",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "output_dir = Path(\"raw/\")\n",
    "output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "for url in pdf_links:\n",
    "    filename = Path(urlparse(url).path).name\n",
    "    download(url, output_dir / filename)"
   ]
  },
